[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789624592","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105175#issuecomment-2789624592","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105175","id":2789624592,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mRksQ","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T13:00:02Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T13:00:13Z","body":"I changed my mind slightly about how we should handle this. While this solves pipeline stutters, it won't solve any other stutters caused by screen buffer creation when the element suddenly appears. Something about where this was placed breaks the regular flow of where this behavior is usually handled.\r\n\r\nI think what we need is some sort of way to build a default scene state based on tracking what geometry surfaces were created (and also deleted). Said default values would be grabbed here instead of always false:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/a9c7578b30e47be1a01ad7f4e8f53b73b73bf009/servers/rendering/renderer_rd/forward_clustered/render_forward_clustered.cpp#L881-L885\r\n\r\nThat way, we can avoid the current stutters that are caused by the sudden creation of resources when something that uses the effect comes into view.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789624592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789636089","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105175#issuecomment-2789636089","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105175","id":2789636089,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mRnf5","user":{"login":"DarioSamo","id":538504,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODUwNA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538504?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo","html_url":"https://github.com/DarioSamo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DarioSamo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T13:04:13Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T13:11:41Z","body":"The idea for handling this in a way that is based of the surface geometry is pretty straightforward. Both surface creation and surface deletion must call the same function with an argument to increase or decrease counters.\r\n\r\n```\r\n// adjust_surface_counters must be called after creating a surface and before deleting one.\r\n\r\nvoid adjust_surface_counters(Surface *p_surface, bool p_increase) {\r\n  int counter_change = p_increase ? 1 : -1;\r\n  if (p_surface->flags & USES_SSS) {\r\n    surfaces_state.subsurface_scattering += counter_change;\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  if (p_surface->flags & USES_NORMAL_TEXTURE) {\r\n    surfaces_state.normal_textures += counter_change;\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen the above code can simply do:\r\n```\r\nscene_state.used_sss = surfaces_state.subsurface_scattering > 0; \r\n scene_state.used_normal_texture = surfaces_state.normal_textures > 0; \r\n ```\r\nAnd consequently, this will also enable the pipeline data _and_ create the textures necessary, eliminating both sources of stutter that can happen if either of these elements are out of view.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2789636089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790545262","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105175#issuecomment-2790545262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105175","id":2790545262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mVFdu","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T18:08:21Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T18:08:21Z","body":"@DarioSamo That's a good idea. It will solve https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101554 as well","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790545262/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790752196","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105175#issuecomment-2790752196","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105175","id":2790752196,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mV3_E","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T19:12:36Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T19:26:22Z","body":"> Then the above code can simply do:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> scene_state.used_sss = surfaces_state.subsurface_scattering > 0; \r\n>  scene_state.used_normal_texture = surfaces_state.normal_textures > 0; \r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> And consequently, this will also enable the pipeline data _and_ create the textures necessary, eliminating both sources of stutter that can happen if either of these elements are out of view.\r\n\r\nIt turned out not to be this simple lol. These can trigger behaviour that we only want in frames where it is necessary (like resolving the depth texture etc.). Instead we need to trigger resource + pipeline creation based on the surface data and then still check what is visible per frame for the `scene_state`. A bit more complex unfortunately. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790752196/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790914380","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105175#issuecomment-2790914380","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105175","id":2790914380,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mWflM","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-09T20:21:00Z","updated_at":"2025-04-09T20:21:00Z","body":"Updated! In the end it didn't make sense to track the absolute numbers as all of these resources are created when needed and not freed. \r\n\r\nI originally incremented the counter for each usage and then used the counter to initialize the `scene_state` variables, e.g.\r\n```\r\nscene_state.used_sss = surfaces_state.subsurface_scattering > 0; \r\n```\r\nHowever, that broke rendering in a couple of subtle ways because we were doing things like texture copies unnecessarily. \r\n\r\nWhat I ended up with I think is actually a little bit simpler and should scale well if other resources need this treatment","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2790914380/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2794229540","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105175#issuecomment-2794229540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105175","id":2794229540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mjI8k","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users